==Services==
The airline provides several tiers of service. ''Imperial First'' is available on long-haul aircraft and features ''The High Ground'' suites, which are fully enclosed private pods equipped with large 4K screens and a Satori-assisted concierge. ''Diamond Business'' offers a staggered layout with direct aisle access and fully flat beds. The ''Premium Green'' cabin is designed for technocratic sector travelers, providing a dedicated check-in and increased seat pitch. The ''Ordinary'' economy class features a 34-inch seat pitch and universal power outlets at every seat.

In-flight entertainment is delivered through the ''Avatar System'', which offers over 1,500 hours of content and high-speed satellite Wi-Fi known as ''Satori Sky-Sync''. The dining program, titled ''Spiceworks'', caters to local preferences for piquant flavors, featuring ''Kaiseki'' meals and a specialized ''Karai Signature'' menu of high-heat spicy stews. Premium passengers also have access to the ''Imperial Suite'' and ''Diamond Lounge'' networks, which include amenities such as bonsai forests and soundproof sleep-cells.

